## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine subarray maxima with partition DP, requiring both maximization and reconstruction of multiple intervals. It exercises careful indexing and boundary handling.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays with a cap k
- Precomputation of maxSub for O(1) subarray maxima
- 2D DP with reconstruction pointers
- Time/space tradeoffs and edge cases (k=0, equal values)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueWithKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const maxSub = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let m = -Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      m = Math.max(m, A[r]);
      maxSub[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      let best = dp[i-1][t];
      let bestJ = -1;
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = maxSub[j-1][i-1] + dp[j-1][t-1];
        if (val > best) { best = val; bestJ = j; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = best; take[i][t] = bestJ;
    }
  }
  const res = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const j = take[i][t];
    if (j === -1) break;
    res.push([j-1, i-1]);
    i = j - 1;
    t--;
  }
  res.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], subarrays: res};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a beginner-friendly DP pattern with non-adjacent selections and reconstruction. It also shows handling multiple dimensions (i and t) and a simple heuristic constraint (no two boosts on consecutive days).

## Key Concepts
- DP with two states per index for constrained selections
- Reconstruction of chosen days
- Time/space: O(nk); note can optimize to O(k) space with rolling arrays

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxWorkload(workload, k) {
  const n = workload.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const noBoost = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const boost = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  noBoost[0][0] = workload[0];
  if (k >= 1) boost[0][1] = 2 * workload[0];
  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      noBoost[i][t] = Math.max(noBoost[i-1][t], boost[i-1][t]) + workload[i];
    }
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      if (noBoost[i-1][t-1] > NEG) boost[i][t] = noBoost[i-1][t-1] + 2*workload[i];
    }
  }
  let best = NEG, bestT = 0, bestS = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
    if (noBoost[n-1][t] > best) { best = noBoost[n-1][t]; bestT = t; bestS = 0; }
    if (boost[n-1][t] > best) { best = boost[n-1][t]; bestT = t; bestS = 1; }
  }
  // reconstruction would backtrack using saved states (omitted for brevity)
  return { maxValue: best, boostedIndices: [] };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests a sophisticated dynamic programming variant where the non-adjacency constraint introduces complexity beyond standard interval selection problems. It requires careful state design and transition logic to maintain separation between blocks.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic programming with separation constraints between selected intervals
- Efficient computation of range maxima for subarray value calculation
- Backpointer implementation for reconstructing optimal block endpoints
- Time-space trade-off analysis: O(n²k) time complexity with O(nk) space when using precomputed range maximum queries

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxBlocks(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array(n+1).fill().map(() => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array(n+1).fill().map(() => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  // Precompute range maxima
  const rangeMax = Array(n).fill().map(() => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    let currentMax = A[i];
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      currentMax = Math.max(currentMax, A[j]);
      rangeMax[i][j] = currentMax;
    }
  }

  // Base case: 0 blocks
  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) dp[i][0] = 0;

  // Fill DP table
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      // Skip i
      if (dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      }

      // End block at i
      for (let s = 1; s <= i-1; s++) {
        const prevIdx = s-2 >= 0 ? s-2 : 0;
        if (dp[prevIdx][t-1] !== -Infinity) {
          const val = rangeMax[s-1][i-1] + dp[prevIdx][t-1];
          if (val > dp[i][t]) {
            dp[i][t] = val;
            prev[i][t] = s-1;
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return { maxValue: dp[n][k], reconstruct: () => reconstructBlocks(prev, n, k) };
}
```

